story.append(Spacer(1,34));para('WALKTHRU · ENGINEERING CASE STUDY','SubAudit')
story.append(Paragraph('When the browser succeeds<br/>but the agent cannot finish',styles['TitleAudit']))
para('An instrumented audit of LangGraph state, browser actions, completion proofs, report generation and SEO/GEO claims.')
para('13 November 2026 | Live public websites | Free model chain | Evidence edition')
figure(EVID/'portfolio/frames/step-02.jpg','Figure 1. Baseline portfolio step 2 reached the Walkthru project detail page. The graph still recorded zero completed checkpoints.',maxh=295)
sub('Abstract')
para('Three baseline journeys were run against Portfolio, Scribb and Tripverse and saved privately in the requested Walkthru account. All three ended without confirmed completion. The traces distinguish observed browser progress from the graph’s completion contract: a blank navigation matcher, invented route expectations, a navigation task typed as a functional outcome, and an off-screen target selected despite an explicit visibility flag. These failures can occur even when browser controls work. The report pipeline often limits the resulting harm by withholding unsupported UX findings. Separate deterministic SEO/GEO rules still make some claims stronger than their measurements justify. Controlled follow-ups and replay checks test the most direct repair, while preserving raw prompts, state snapshots, tool results and screenshot evidence.')

head('1. Scope, method and reproducibility')
para('This is a small engineering case study, not a benchmark of general model reliability. The evaluator selected representative visitor goals; the user supplied the three sites and authorized saving runs in their account. The pricing goal for Scribb was not verified as an offered feature before the first run. That limits conclusions about task feasibility; it does not invalidate the observed planner and visibility defects. A second Scribb goal uses the Demo Journal control observed during the baseline.')
para('The local cloud-runner implementation launched disposable headless Chromium sessions and loaded the repository’s built inject.js. It called the normal run-admission, graph-resume, screenshot-storage and report-persistence logic. Real free models chose actions. Existing server-side verification and visitor restrictions remained in force. A temporary development Plus entitlement enabled all three domains without payment; the evaluation scripts revoke their longer-lived temporary passes on completion.')
para('The harness called internal API handlers rather than exercising browser login, HTTP authentication, cloud queue leasing or the deployed worker. The report job was captured and executed in the same instrumented process. Its actual report graph, scans and database writes ran. Thus the evidence establishes application-logic execution and private saved runs, not production deployment acceptance. Report email was disabled. The supplied email was used to identify the account and is omitted from this publication copy.')
para('Captured artifacts include every application-level browser snapshot/act/evidence call, every model prompt and parsed response, provider attempts, graph node inputs/outputs, proof checks, post-action JPEGs, selected pre-action aim frames, final graph state and saved report JSON. Diagnostic follow-ups additionally log synchronous httpx method, URL path, status and latency. Baseline network transport was not fully traced; browser subresource requests and all asynchronous provider traffic are not a complete packet capture. Screenshots document rendered UI; they are not what the controller model saw.')
para('LangGraph interrupt callbacks are logged as node_error by the generic callback. Interrupt(value=...) in these logs is the expected pause before the browser acts, not a failed node. A resumed act node starts again and returns once its observation arrives. Counting these starts as independent clicks would double-count tool execution.')
para('The repository was dirty before the audit and contained ongoing cloud-runner work. source-manifest.json records the inspected source hashes and Git base; function-inventory.json indexes declarations and statically observed calls. An index entry does not mean the function executed. The paper identifies runtime-observed facts separately from source-review findings and proposed changes. The full HTML appendix preserves exact evidence and account report IDs.')

head('2. Results and saved runs')
rows=[['Run / condition','Terminal state','Steps','Elapsed journey','Report']]
for r in manifest:rows.append([r['slug'],r.get('status','?'),str(r.get('steps','?')),str(r['journey_seconds'])+' s','saved' if r.get('report_ready') else 'missing'])
table(rows,[150,90,45,105,105])
para('Step counts are saved decision records, including a terminal give_up where present. Journey elapsed time includes browser setup, admission, provider waits and persistence; the report phase follows it. The three baselines are not interchangeable tasks and the follow-ups are diagnostic experiments, not repeated trials. No success-rate estimate is warranted.')
for r in manifest:
 para(r['slug']+': '+r['goal'],'SmallAudit');para('Saved report: /app/runs/'+r['run_id'],'SmallAudit')
para('Two early attempts ended before a saved run was created: portfolio browser startup failed once, and Tripverse hit the original two-site entitlement limit. Those are admission/startup incidents, not agent task failures. The first browser exception was not captured in enough detail to assign a root cause. A retry reached the website successfully.')
para('The application selects the active entitlement with the latest expiry, not necessarily the highest plan. A one-day Plus grant was initially outranked by the existing longer Pro pass. The audit therefore used a specifically identified longer development entitlement and revoked that row after the experiment. This behavior deserves an entitlement-selection regression test; it is distinct from model quality.')
head('2a. Follow-ups that refine the diagnosis')
para('The first portfolio intervention reused /dial/ routes from the baseline, but a fresh visit to the homepage redirected to /ledger/. The browser again opened a project detail; the reused predicates rejected it. The controller even tried switching themes to satisfy the stale route. This is a failed intervention and direct evidence that route grounding must be scoped to the current run, not copied from an earlier theme. The final controlled experiment starts explicitly at the observed /dial/ route to isolate predicate validity; it is not a test of autonomous route discovery.')
para('The supported Scribb follow-up opened Demo Journal at step 2, revisited it at step 5, and ended agent_lost at step 6. Its last checkpoint was outcome with neither a route nor text expectation. This removes the baseline pricing-feasibility ambiguity: even an available, successfully opened feature could not satisfy the generated contract.')
para('The final portfolio experiment starts at /dial/ and replaces the generated plan with navigation predicates for /dial/projects.html and /dial/work.html. Both come from the baseline browser evidence. The real controller and validator then complete the task in two steps, confirming both milestones. In contrast, the baseline reaches the same detail route but never advances its null-matcher first checkpoint. The experiment demonstrates that valid predicates can remove this specific blockage; autonomous discovery of those predicates still needs implementation.')
table([['Comparison','What it establishes','What it does not establish'],['Baseline vs recorded replay','The recorded transitions can satisfy grounded navigation predicates.','No new model behavior is tested by replay.'],['Baseline vs /ledger/ intervention','A stale route copied from another theme remains a bad contract.','Not evidence that the site must use /dial/.'],['Baseline vs fixed /dial/ run','Same goal, valid predicates and a matched start route completed in two actions.','Not a population success rate or general autonomous repair.'],['Scribb pricing vs Demo Journal','An available journal flow also exposes outcome misclassification.','No conclusion that a pricing page exists or is missing site-wide.']], [130,185,180])
para('Provider fallbacks varied across attempts. Temperature zero does not make the environment deterministic: redirects, public content, timing and provider availability can change. The scripts log those differences rather than hiding failed interventions. A release decision still needs repeated trials with fixed tasks and negative completion controls.')

head('3. The complete execution path')
para('There are two LangGraph graphs. Goal planning, admission, browser execution, storage and job dispatch surround them. Treating every service as a graph node obscures which component actually decides the next step.')
table([['Stage','Input -> output / implementation'],['Admission','Account, site, goal, plan and policy -> authorized run; main._start_run, plans, quotes, reservations, ownership checks.'],['Planner','Goal + initial rendered text snapshot (5,000-character cut) -> GoalPlan; goal.plan, runtime.call(GoalPlan).'],['Persona graph','START -> decide. decide -> act for browser actions; decide -> check for done/give_up. act -> check. check -> decide if running, otherwise END.'],['Browser boundary','act interrupts with step. Runner calls inject.js, captures screenshot and fresh snapshot, then main._observe resumes with observation/evidence/action_id.'],['Completion','goal.evidence checks ordered public milestones. check updates plan_done and proof list; safety, budget and repetition rules can terminate.'],['Report handoff','_finish_later serializes selected graph state into finish_run job. finish_run reads saved run, rechecks verification and invokes report graph.'],['Report graph','START fans out to first_impression, accessibility_scan, site_scan, stack_scan. site_scan -> performance_scan. All four branch ends join synthesize -> END.'],['Persistence / viewing','db.set_report, private evidence Storage, in-app notification, optional email; React report reads saved account data.']], [110,385])
para('Editable complete architecture: walkthru-agent-flowchart.excalidraw and its SVG export. The companion walkthru-agent.excalidraw contains the deeper state/context panels. live-traces.excalidraw adds the observed failure paths. These are source-inspection maps; only the recorded paths in the appendix are asserted as executed.')

head('4. What survives from the previous state')
table([['State / context','What the next decision receives','Limit or consequence'],['goal + plan','Original objective, planner intent, ordered checklist and declared evidence matchers.','The current checklist item dominates action selection even when its predicate is impossible.'],['plan_done + proof','Code-owned completion count; proof entries also appear in history.','Model progress is overwritten. An earlier unprovable checkpoint blocks later proofs.'],['observation','Current URL/title, errors/notices, controls with IDs/context/visibility, scroll containers, executor result, public text.','Text is cut to 4,000 characters; snapshots have bounded element/context coverage. No screenshot pixels enter this controller.'],['steps / render_history','Last eight factual actions; old milestones and up to four earlier unresolved actions; bounded to 6,000 characters.','Target labels are stored but absent from the usual rendered history. Old #IDs are document-local and can be misleading after navigation.'],['Policy and persona','Verified/visitor constraints, task priority, test identity, persona preferences.','Instructions say not to select hidden controls, but selection is still unconstrained model output.'],['Memory / checkpoint','run_id thread plus LangGraph saver retains state across interrupts; default in-memory or configured Postgres saver.','Persistence is not semantic repair. A saved invalid plan remains invalid. No vector recall/RAG is used in this loop.'],['Report payload','status, steps, tokens, first_text, plan; final observation reduced to controls.','Full final snapshot and intermediate states are not passed to the report. Source review found assertion fields omitted at this boundary.']], [90,205,200])
para('The central defect is not simply “too little memory.” The controller receives fresh page data, but it also receives a stale or unprovable instruction to keep working on the current checkpoint. The proof function returns only a proof object or None. The next prompt lacks a structured explanation such as missing_navigation_marker, route_mismatch, or missing_outcome_expectation, and lacks a defined repair transition.')
sub('Expected state repair')
para('Add code-owned checkpoint validation and proof diagnostics before another decision: checkpoint_id, evidence_kind, provenance, last_observation_revision, match_result, rejection_reason, attempted_action_signature and recovery_count. Preserve the original goal. A missing expectation should enter needs_expectation or bounded discovery, not a normal execution loop. A genuinely observed navigation destination may be bound from an observed link or selected target; it must not be invented from its label.')

head('5. External services and tool boundaries')
table([['Component','Role and evidence boundary'],['Chromium + CDP + inject.js','Browser renders public site; snapshot/redact extracts text and controls; execute applies one action; axe and web-vitals capture browser diagnostics. JPEGs are evidence, not controller vision.'],['Groq','Observed baseline successes use openai/gpt-oss-120b and openai/gpt-oss-20b. Rate-limit errors triggered fallback. Exact provider attempts and timing appear in events.'],['Gemini / OpenRouter','Configured fallback alternatives in runtime.free_pool; availability does not prove use. OpenRouter is inserted for writer calls when configured. Consult per-run provider events.'],['Jev / paid candidates','Optional decision adapters in source. This evaluation forces the existing LLM/free path and disables paid candidate settings. No conclusion about Jev or Claude follows from these runs.'],['Supabase / Postgres','Account lookup, entitlements, run rows, private screenshot objects, report rows and notifications. LangGraph saver is a separate persistence concern.'],['Site HTTP / robots / sitemap','Shared SSRF-safe bounded crawler feeds SEO, GEO and passive hygiene. Coverage and failures must be read per report. No repository source is fetched.'],['PageSpeed Insights / CrUX','Optional performance integration; missing service results may coexist with browser vitals. checks.performance=complete is not evidence of a successful Lighthouse response.'],['DNS-over-HTTPS','Email DNS and other passive DNS checks; a DNS observation is not a delivery test or evidence of an exploit.'],['LangSmith / usage ledger','Optional tracing and provider accounting infrastructure. Local audit events are the evidence of record here; no claim that every span arrived in LangSmith.'],['Resend / Dodo','Email delivery and billing integrations exist outside the task loop. Report email was suppressed; no payment was submitted.']], [130,365])

findings=[
('F1 / P0','Planner emits unprovable checkpoints','Observed in all baselines. Portfolio checkpoint 1 is navigation with no URL matcher; checkpoint 2 is outcome with no text expectation. Tripverse invents /destinations for an in-page section. Scribb invents /pricing and marks a page-opening goal as outcome with null text.','goal.plan; goal.evidence; schema.GoalPlan; persona.system_prompt','Validate a typed navigation/section/functional contract before execution. Ground hrefs in observed controls (currently the controller element model does not expose destinations). Represent same-page section visibility separately from business outcomes. Preserve unknown functional expectations as unknown. Add bounded discovery or request owner expectations when needed.','Recorded portfolio replay must accept the two real navigation transitions with grounded predicates; missing or invented matchers must never be run as a normal current checkpoint. Negative test: a generic toast or mere scroll cannot prove signup/send/save.'),
('F2 / P0','Proof rejection is lost before the next decision','Portfolio reached its detail page at step 2 but plan_done stayed zero. The next prompt demanded checkpoint 1 again; later visits tripped looping.','persona.act/check; goal.evidence; render_history','Return structured proof reasons and add a bounded plan-repair branch. Distinguish completed destination, missing expectation, route mismatch, execution refusal and unobserved effect. Do not ask the model to overwrite proof counts.','Using the recorded step-2 state, the next decision must receive the rejected predicate and reason and must not revisit Projects solely to satisfy an impossible plan.'),
('F3 / P1','Off-screen choice terminates without recovery','Scribb selected #22 About while in_view=false after scrolling. _enforce replaced the click with give_up and agent_lost. The refusal is safe; the missing recovery makes the agent brittle.','persona._enforce; render_observation; extension snapshot/navigation','Filter executable targets to current visible unobstructed controls, or reject with structured feedback and one bounded scroll/reobserve recovery. Recheck revision and visibility after movement. Never dispatch the refused click blindly.','Replay the saved Scribb choice: no hidden click executes; one bounded observation/navigation recovery is allowed; repeated failure terminates as agent limitation.'),
('F4 / P1','Loop signature includes parameters irrelevant to clicks','Tripverse clicked Destinations ten times. scroll_container_id alternated null and 0, although the action was click. Once three consecutive signatures matched, check returned stuck.','persona.check: keys built for tail; _lost','Normalize action signatures by action type. For click use stable current-document target identity/label and outcome fingerprint; omit scroll/wait options. Track repeated attempts against the same unresolved checkpoint and unchanged semantic result.','Equivalent clicks differing only by scroll_container_id must count toward one retry limit. Real list scrolling and changed content must not be mistaken for repeated clicks.'),
('F5 / P1','Report wording sometimes exceeds deterministic evidence','SEO says missing alt makes images invisible to search engines; thin content “rarely” ranks; GEO turns paragraph-length tests into semantic claims. These strings come from code, not a hallucinatory report model.','scans/seo.py; seo_depth.py; geo.py; email.py','Separate observed measurement, heuristic interpretation and verified impact. Replace absolute claims; label GEO scoring advisory. Preserve existing honest uncertainty for optional AI text files. Do not infer email failure from absent MX alone.','Golden report fixtures must distinguish absent attribute/low word count from ranking prediction, citation likelihood, actual mail failure or verified site defect.'),
('F6 / P1','Report handoff drops declared assertion fields','Source-review finding: _finish_later keeps status/steps/tokens/first_text/plan; finish_run reads assertion/assertion_outcome from the payload. These visitor runs did not exercise owner assertions.','main._finish_later and main.finish_run','Include validated assertion and assertion_outcome in the persisted job contract; add a job round-trip test. Preserve missing-as-unknown semantics.','Queue an owner assertion run, deserialize its report job and verify the exact expectation/outcome reaches assessment without inference.'),
('F7 / P2','Observability can misidentify error, cost and provider','Expected LangGraph interrupts look like node errors in a generic callback; legacy report tokens omit the planner call; report.model is a configured label rather than proof of the model that answered.','runtime.call/guarded; goal.plan; report.synthesize; provider_usage','Emit explicit interrupt/resume spans, stage/provider/model receipts and complete token accounting. Keep successful and failed provider attempts separate. Prefer receipts over nominal model labels.','One live run must reconcile planner + decisions + first impression + synthesis usage, including fallback attempts, and distinguish expected pauses from errors.'),
('F8 / P1','Synthesis amplifies scanner claims in the summary','The successful portfolio report says accessibility violations block screen readers and AI crawlers see empty pages. The audit did not test every assistive technology or answer engine.','report.SYNTHESIS_SYSTEM; synthesize; summary/top_fixes contract','Carry evidence scope and uncertainty into every summary assertion, not only ux_findings. Use evidence-bound summary items or deterministic rendering for categorical measurements.','Given the saved final report inputs, no summary may convert a static heuristic or scoped axe finding into a universal user-impact claim; every impact statement must have an appropriate supporting source.')]
head('6. Exact fixes, evidence and acceptance criteria')
para('The following changes are proposed engineering work. The audit harness does not ship them into product source. Priority reflects ability to explain these failures, not a claim about every failure in production.')
for ident,title,evidence,location,fix,test in findings:
 sub(ident+' · '+title);para('Evidence: '+evidence);para('Location: '+location,'SmallAudit');para('Change: '+fix);para('Acceptance: '+test,'SmallAudit')

head('7. Prompt audit: planning, decisions and reports')
table([['Prompt stage','What was actually provided','Assessment'],['GoalPlan','Original goal + rendered initial snapshot; planner prompt allows null expectations when unknown.','Good: avoids inventing finish phrases in its text rule. Gap: null and guessed URL predicates still pass into an execution checklist. The code grounds text_contains but not url_contains.'],['PersonaStep','System objective/checklist/persona/safety + bounded factual history/current snapshot; one correction for unsupported done/give_up.','Good: original objective is authoritative and progress is code-owned. Gap: no proof rejection reason, missing href provenance, all visible/offscreen IDs offered in one list, no repair transition.'],['FirstImpression','Up to 5,000 characters of first page text; instructions prohibit visual/layout/color claims.','This is a text impression, not a screenshot design review. First page may be a redirect destination. Keep the input type explicit.'],['Synthesis','Measured findings, final controls, journey facts, scope and evidence references; grounded_ux filters supported issues.','Baseline runs skipped the model when unfinished without observed failure and used a deterministic summary. That protection worked.'],['SEO / GEO','There is no dedicated SEO or GEO model prompt in this graph. Scanners produce findings and scores from HTTP/HTML/robots/schema data.','Prompt-only changes will not repair misleading scanner strings or score assumptions. Fix the deterministic rule and evidence contract.']], [90,205,200])
para('Full exact prompts and parsed outputs are in trace-appendix.html. These are observable model I/O, including the returned think-aloud field; they are not access to a model’s hidden reasoning. The follow-up planner substitution is recorded explicitly as experimental_intervention, with the original proposal and replacement.')
sub('Proposed controller input contract')
para('Owner objective; current validated checkpoint; evidence provenance; completion predicate; last action and actual effect; rejection reason; executable targets; other visible sections; unresolved safe alternatives; recovery budget. Keep page text marked untrusted. Give the model an explicit recover/reobserve choice when an action is refused, while code retains authority over safety and completion.')

head('8. SEO, GEO and report interpretation')
para('The baseline reports saved 22 findings for Portfolio, 15 for Scribb and 17 for Tripverse. These are rule outputs, not 54 independently proven defects. Reports correctly kept UX findings empty and said completion was unconfirmed. Browser LCP/CLS were identified as single-visit measurements, distinct from population field data or Lighthouse. These are useful grounding controls.')
table([['Claim under review','What the measurement supports','Required wording / reference'],['Missing alt -> images invisible to search','An img attribute is absent in fetched HTML.','Say that useful text alternatives are missing. Google also uses computer vision and page content. [R1]'],['Low word count -> pages rarely rank','Fetched HTML contains approximately N words.','Report scope and possible content gap, not a ranking prediction. Google has no magical word-count target. [R2]'],['No long early paragraph -> no plain answer','A length threshold on the first paragraphs failed.','Label it a formatting heuristic. It does not establish whether the text answers a question or will be cited.'],['Optional AI text files','File absent or HTML returned.','The existing “effect not established” qualification is appropriate. Google requires no special AI text files for its AI features. [R3]'],['No MX -> domain cannot receive email','No MX response from the resolver.','Do not assert delivery failure; SMTP defines an implicit MX fallback to the host when no MX records exist. [R4]'],['No og:title -> no title or image preview','Only the og:title selector is absent.','Check title/description/image independently; report absent metadata, not guaranteed platform output.'],['High GEO/launch score -> successful task','Rule-weighted readiness scores over sampled pages.','Keep task completion, indexability, citation visibility and advisory score separate. Scribb scored 95 GEO while the journey ended agent_lost.']], [120,175,200])
para('These source-based corrections do not prove a particular site ranks, receives mail, or appears in AI answers. They narrow the claims to what was measured. Primary references were consulted on 13 November 2026; only short paraphrases are used. Google guidance here applies to Google Search, not every answer engine.')
para('The successful matched-route run did invoke Synthesis. Its summary says accessibility violations “block screen readers” and that AI crawlers and link previews see empty pages. Those broad impacts were not directly tested. This shows a second amplification boundary: even when the journey is correctly marked done, a writer can turn scoped scanner findings into categorical impact statements. Require the synthesis summary to preserve the same uncertainty and scope as each evidence source; filtering ux_findings alone does not constrain every sentence in summary or top_fixes.')

head('9. Observed traces and screenshots')
para('Each run below includes its exact planner contract, terminal interpretation, provider attempts and every saved step. The image on a step page is its post-action frame; pre-action aim frames are available in the HTML appendix. Terminal decisions may have only a final captured view. A frame is evidence of the viewport at capture time, not proof of backend state.')
para('For complete input/output data at every node, expand the corresponding event in trace-appendix.html. JSONL event order records callback arrival; concurrent report branches can overlap. Explicit node invocation IDs connect starts and ends. Screenshot hashes are listed in evidence-hashes.json.')
trace_image=PILImage.open(OUT/'live-traces.png')
for name,x in [('Portfolio',0),('Scribb',570),('Tripverse',1140)]:
 head(name+' / observed graph path')
 target=OUT/(name.lower()+'-trace.png');trace_image.crop((x,85,min(x+540,trace_image.width),1280)).save(target)
